# The Kali archive, as it ships in the installed `security` image.
#
# The installed system needs this source for the same reason the build chroot
# did: a metapackage whose members came from here can only be upgraded from
# here. Removing it would leave the tools unfixable - `apt-get upgrade` would
# not see the newer versions, and samurai-recovery restore-packages compares
# against a package list an archive can no longer satisfy.
#
# Shipping it is not the same as trusting it for automatic changes:
# unattended-upgrades is configured with Allowed-Origins "Debian:trixie-security"
# only (etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20samurai-security), so nothing from this archive is
# ever upgraded without the user asking. That is the trade this variant makes,
# and samurai/docs/known-limitations.md states it as a limitation rather than a
# feature: Kali-sourced tools receive no automatic security patches.
deb [ arch=amd64 ] https://archive.kali.org/kali kali-rolling main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
